// (prior ship record) var Version = "1.46.0" // THE CLEAN MIND SHIP (PLAN-V146, the user's report verbatim: "the pm native reasoning shows duplicate texts. Every word appears twice in it's reasoning for some reason… I'm not sure what else uve missed in that regard. But it seems native can still use some work"). THE WAVE: the duplicate-reasoning bug root-caused and fixed live + the missed reasoning ledger surfaced. v1.46.1 THE ALIAS LAW — live-probed against the real deployment (glm-5.3 + gpt-oss-120b, plain + tool rounds, streaming + non-streaming): PM's gateway (system_fingerprint vllm-0.31.0-tp4) emits EVERY reasoning delta in BOTH wire spellings byte-equal ('{"reasoning":"The","reasoning_content":"The"}' — the vLLM compat shim for the channel rename "reasoning used to be called reasoning_content", docs.vllm.ai); the engine's v1.14.6 normalization merged Reasoning+ReasoningOR on the assumption "only one shape is ever non-empty per chunk in practice" — convicted FALSE for PM: every word of PM-native reasoning doubled ("TheThe user user asks asks…"). reasoning.go gains mergeWireReasoning — the two spellings are DOCUMENTED ALIASES of ONE channel: byte-equal pair = ONE copy; single-spelling senders (OpenRouter reasoning / NIM reasoning_content) byte-identical to before; a both-non-empty-and-different delta keeps the historical concatenation so no wire byte is ever dropped; both chat.go merge sites consume the merge; reasoning_v1461_test.go pins the LIVE-CAPTURED frames byte-for-byte. RED-TEAMED LIVE: the pre-fix flip through the full engine reproduces the user's exact symptom (adjacent-duplicate rate 0.47: "TheThe user user asks asks:: What What is is 2 2++22?? Answer Answer in in one one word word.."); the fix streams clean (rate 0.000–0.036 across repeated live runs). v1.46.2 THE REASONING LEDGER — the live capture showed glm-5.3 spending 53 of 56 completion tokens REASONING for a one-word answer while the LEDGER dropped the detail (completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens parsed nowhere): llm.Usage gains ReasoningTokens (0 = unreported, never invented); the per-chunk overwrite keeps the final's honest numbers; mergeUsage SUMS across tool rounds from birth (the v1.44.6 TotalTokens lesson); the live event + persisted status usage + both usage endpoints (session totals + per-model + fleet per-provider + grand) carry the share; the usage panel renders the 🧠 thinking-tokens stat + per-model/provider chips (theme tokens only; old sessions parse 0 — additive, no migration). v1.46.3 THE PROOF — pmlive gate TestLivePMReasoningClean (a REAL glm-5.3 turn through the engine's own pipeline: no doubled words rate<0.20, the answer intact, usage carries the reasoning share; the RELIABLE reasoning trigger "Think step by step: 17×23" forced the channel 3/3 in the empirical probe — bare "2+2" reasoned only 2/3, a flaky gate is a lying gate) + scripts/v1460-clean-mind-rig.py 16/16 (RA the alias law live through the engine's own WS chat protocol with a real browser page + real key; RB the ledger live end-to-end; RC the source pins) + regressions ALL GREEN (v1350 62/62, v1400 51+27+58, v1440 27/27, v1450 26/26, go battery 14/14, all pmlive gates) + the UI-driven agent-browser pass (the thinking bubble renders undoubled — rate 0.022; the usage panel shows 🧠 54; /api/sessions/:id/usage answers reasoningTokens 54 of 58 output). Honest limits: glm's dynamic reasoning SKIPS recall facts intermittently (the capital-of-France prompt reasoned 0/2 — the "2+2" prompts 2/3+2/2) — the gates use the empirically-forced trigger; old persisted sessions keep their historical (possibly doubled) thinking text — history is never rewritten, new turns are clean.
// (prior ship record) var Version = "1.45.0" // THE HONEST PM SHIP (PLAN-V145, the user's report verbatim: "the bugger bug is pm is unreachable and flags network falsely… PM should work like the rest without the need for a separate bridge sandbox… each chat should be isolated and have its own instance completely"). The wave: the two bugs the user's device test convicted, root-caused and fixed. v1.45.1 THE ANDROID WIRE — the vendored PM client dialed with Go's DEFAULT dialer while every other engine outbound rides netx.DialContext (the engine's own law: "the Android DNS fix applies everywhere") — on Android there is no /etc/resolv.conf, Go's pure resolver is unreliable, so PM was the ONE provider that died on real devices while Nvidia/OpenRouter streamed (the user's "network unreachable… even tho I was connected to the internet"); pmstate now wires netx.Transport() (which also drops the vendored 5s HTTP/2 health-check ping that killed mid-request connections on lossy mobile links); PROVENANCE delta 8; TestManagerDialsViaNetx pins the law. v1.45.2 THE HONEST NET — the two outage shapes get opposite honesty: PROVIDER-SCOPED (another provider's recent success is positive evidence the network works — RecordProviderSuccess stamps LastSuccessAt, anyOtherProviderHealthy consults it): the texts NEVER blame "network" ("PrivateMode is unreachable — retrying in Ns (your connection is fine)"), and netProviderHoldLoop is a BOUNDED hold (DOOMALAY_PROVIDER_HOLD_MS, prod 2min) ending in the honest provider-down verdict with the lock released (the old infinite suspension held the session hostage — every fresh send hit "busy"); DEVICE-OFFLINE (no success evidence): the v1.39.3 patient engine byte-for-byte (infinite suspension, wake channel, the honest "network" texts). The hiccup counter tells the truth (the old hardcoded "/2" counted past itself live). pmstate drift-checks pinned-CA INIT failures (a corrupt/rotated pin convicts with ErrPMDeploymentChanged, never a net-loop). v1.45.3